=== meta ===
rule: CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED
issue: 419
title: A Makefile that builds instead of testing is production, and still earns repair evidence for a rewritten expected value
origin: FP guard for the 2026-08-11 runner widening — filename must not decide this, content must
origin2: Kept under this name by the #419 ruling (issuecomment-6170353038: Q6 (a), rule 2) for the
origin3: expectation family; the weakened assertion it pinned until then moved, same inputs, to
origin4: runner_build_makefile_pos. The exact count still forbids CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED.
=== before: Makefile ===
libfast.so: fast.c
	$(CC) -O2 -shared -o libfast.so fast.c
=== after: Makefile ===
libfast.so: fast.c
	$(CC) -O3 -shared -fPIC -o libfast.so fast.c
=== before: tests/test_billing.py ===
from billing import invoice_total


def test_total():
    assert invoice_total([50.0, 50.0], 0.05) == 100.0
=== after: tests/test_billing.py ===
from billing import invoice_total


def test_total():
    assert invoice_total([50.0, 50.0], 0.05) == 105.0
=== expect ===
[{"rule": "EXPECTED_VALUE_CHANGED", "severity": "warn", "deescalators": ["REPAIR_EVIDENCE"]}]
